Root cause:
The bug was caused by the improper initialization of the `riscv_cbom_block_size` variable, which was set to a default value of `L1_CACHE_BYTES`. This default value was not guaranteed to be valid across all RISC-V systems, as the ISA does not mandate a specific cache block size. Additionally, the warning handling for uninitialized hart IDs could trigger erroneously, leading to misleading warnings. The patch corrects these issues by ensuring that the block size is only set after probing the actual hardware configuration, thus preventing incorrect assumptions about the cache block size.
